ZkPassportMethodFuzzTest
├── when the initial keys are fewer than eight
│   └── it should revert
├── when the initial keys are more than eight
│   └── it should revert
├── when an initial address word has upper bytes set
│   └── it should revert
├── when the key admin sets fewer than eight words
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets more than eight words
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets a zero in any word but the guardian
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets an address word with upper bytes set
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets a clean address in any address word
│   └── it should store the word as given
├── when the key admin sets a version word with any nonzero padding
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should keep the previous words
├── when the key admin sets a canonical version word for any release
│   └── it should store the word as given
├── when the config carries any identifier domain scope and validity
│   └── it should pass them to the root verifier unchanged
├── when the root returns any identifier other than the configured one
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when the input at length minus three is any nonzero value
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when the input at length minus three is zero
│   └── it should accept the proof
├── when custom data is the lowercase rendering of any digest
│   └── it should accept the proof
├── when custom data renders a different digest
│   └── it should refuse the proof
├── when custom data is the uppercase rendering of a digest starting with a letter
│   └── it should refuse the proof
└── when the snapshot words hold any values
    └── it should accept the proof
